From e45786de49f8c9f1009fbcbd8ab85c05665b9b44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 06:02:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add cursor-driven 3D hero (Three.js) and fix ScrollTrigger
 drift

- Add lib/three-hero-scene.ts: a small vanilla Three.js scene (faceted
  icosahedron + wireframe shell) that follows the cursor, with resize
  observer, visibility pausing, prefers-reduced-motion support, and
  proper dispose() cleanup.
- Add components/hero/three-hero.tsx client wrapper, loaded via
  next/dynamic with ssr:false since it touches window/WebGL.
- Restructure the homepage hero into a two-column layout (copy + 3D
  canvas) and add its entrance to the existing GSAP timeline.
- Replace the hand-rolled useLayoutEffect + gsap.context pattern with
  the official @gsap/react useGSAP hook on all three animated pages
  (home, about, contact). This is the maintained, Strict-Mode-safe
  integration path from GreenSock and avoids the duplicate/dead
  ScrollTrigger instances that pattern can produce across React's
  dev-mode mount->unmount->mount cycle.
- Refresh ScrollTrigger after window 'load' and document.fonts.ready
  in lib/gsap.ts, plus one more rAF-scheduled refresh per page. Web
  fonts finishing their swap after the first layout pass is the most
  common reason trigger start/end points end up wrong (positions
  computed before the page reached its final height).
